    "description": "JOB DESCRIPTION National Sales Manager Job Information Job Title National Sales Manager Department FMCG Division Reports To Commercial Head – FMCG Division Location Head Office Employment Type Full-Time Job Purpose The National Sales Manager is responsible for developing and executing the national sales strategy to achieve revenue growth, market share expansion, and profitability targets. The role leads and manages all sales operations across the country, including upcountry sales, key accounts, field sales, modern trade, sales analytics, and Route-to-Market (RTM) administration. The National Sales Manager ensures effective customer coverage, distributor performance, sales force productivity, and alignment of sales execution with the company's strategic objectives. Key Responsibilities / Accountabilities Strategic Sales Leadership Develop and implement the national sales strategy aligned with the Division's business objectives. Prepare annual sales plans, budgets, and sales forecasts. Identify growth opportunities, new markets, channels, and customer segments. Drive sustainable sales growth and improve market penetration nationwide. Sales Performance Management Lead, supervise, and coach regional and functional sales managers to achieve sales targets. Monitor daily, weekly, and monthly sales performance and implement corrective actions where necessary. Establish sales targets, territory plans, and performance standards. Ensure effective sales execution across all sales channels. Route-to-Market (RTM) Management Develop and optimize the company's Route-to-Market strategy. Improve sales coverage, territory alignment, and customer reach. Ensure efficient van sales operations and route optimization. Monitor distributor performance and route productivity. Key Account & Customer Management Oversee the management of strategic customers, wholesalers, distributors, and modern trade accounts. Build and maintain strong relationships with key customers and business partners. Lead commercial negotiations with major customers. Ensure high levels of customer satisfaction and retention. Sales Operations Ensure effective implementation of sales policies, pricing strategies, promotions, and trade incentives. Monitor product availability and coordinate with Distribution to minimize stock-outs. Collaborate with Marketing to execute promotional campaigns and product launches. Ensure accurate sales forecasting and demand planning. Sales Analytics & Reporting Review sales performance reports and market intelligence. Analyze sales trends, customer buying behavior, and competitor activities. Utilize sales dashboards and KPIs to drive decision-making. Present regular sales performance reports to the General Manager. Team Leadership Recruit, develop, and retain a high-performing sales team. Conduct regular coaching, field visits, and performance reviews. Promote a culture of accountability, customer focus, and continuous improvement. Identify training and development needs for the sales organization. Cross-Functional Collaboration Coordinate with Marketing, Distribution, Finance, and Supply Chain to ensure seamless execution of commercial plans. Support new product launches and expansion initiatives. Participate in strategic planning and business review meetings. Compliance and Governance Ensure adherence to company policies, sales procedures, and ethical standards. Monitor compliance with pricing, credit, and trade promotion policies. Identify and mitigate sales-related risks. Knowledge  FMCG sales and distribution operations.  Route-to-Market (RTM) strategies and channel management.  Distributor and wholesale management.  Key Account Management (KAM).  Modern trade and retail operations.  Sales forecasting and demand planning.  Trade marketing and promotional management.  Pricing and commercial negotiation.  Customer relationship management (CRM).  Sales analytics and performance reporting.  Microsoft Excel, Power BI, and business intelligence tools.  Ethiopian FMCG market dynamics and competitive landscape.",
