    "description": "FAMA is seeking a competent and proactive Legal Officer to manage the company’s legal affairs, support business operations, and help ensure compliance with applicable Ethiopian laws and regulations. Key Responsibilities Contracts and Legal Documents Draft, review, negotiate, and manage contracts, agreements, memorandums of understanding (MOUs), legal notices, and other legal documents. Review tender documents, bid conditions, procurement agreements, subcontract agreements, supplier contracts, and commercial transactions to protect FAMA’s legal interests. Participate in contract negotiations with clients, suppliers, subcontractors, consultants, and business partners. Legal Advice and Compliance Provide legal advice to management and departments on legal, contractual, commercial, procurement, employment, and regulatory matters. Help ensure FAMA complies with applicable Ethiopian labor, commercial, tax, trade, construction, licensing, and other legal requirements. Monitor new laws, regulations, directives, tax updates, and other legislative changes, and advise management on their impact. Conduct legal research and risk assessments, and recommend practical measures to reduce legal and operational risks. Government and Regulatory Matters Represent FAMA before government offices and regulatory authorities when delegated by management. Obtain, renew, and manage business licenses, permits, registrations, certificates, and statutory approvals required for company operations and construction projects. Build and maintain professional relationships with government authorities and external stakeholders. Disputes and Investigations Follow up on legal matters affecting FAMA’s projects and operations, and support their timely resolution. Coordinate litigation, arbitration, claims, and dispute resolution with external legal counsel when required. Coordinate with police and other law enforcement agencies on theft, fraud, project security incidents, traffic accidents, property damage, employee-related legal matters, and other cases affecting company operations. Support internal investigations involving disciplinary matters, fraud, theft, contractual disputes, regulatory violations, or employee misconduct. Correspondence and Communication Draft and review official letters, legal correspondence, notices, responses, and communications with clients, suppliers, subcontractors, consultants, banks, insurance companies, government authorities, and other stakeholders. Ensure external company communications are legally accurate and aligned with company policies. Records, Policies, and Other Duties Maintain accurate and confidential legal records, contracts, permits, licenses, litigation files, and other legal documentation. Develop, review, and update company legal policies, compliance procedures, and standard legal templates. Perform other legal, compliance, administrative, or regulatory duties assigned by management.",
